  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\r\n\r\nI was surprised to see that the `baseURI` property in Chrome returns URLs that include a fragment identifier.\r\n\r\nI think it should be specified that [document base URL](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/urls-and-fetching.html#document-base-url) _should not_ include the fragment identifier.\r\n\r\nThis is because [RFC3986 5.1 states](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc3986#section-5.1):\r\n> A base URI must conform to the `<absolute-URI>` syntax rule ([Section 4.3](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc3986#section-4.3)).  If the base URI is obtained from a URI reference, then that reference must be converted to absolute form and _stripped of any fragment component prior to its use as a base URI_.",
